        {
          "testName": {
            "en": "Related substances"
          },
          "testType": "TestType-Purity",
          "testConditions": {
            "en": "\". Use solution (1) as described thereunder. For solution (2), transfer 25 mg of albendazole RS to a 50 mL volumetric flask. Add 5 mL of sulfuric acid/methanol (1%) TS and immediately dilute to volume with the mobile phase. Inject 5 µL of solutions (1) and (2). The retention time and the size of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with solution (1) correspond to the retention time and the size of the peak due to albendazole in the chromatogram obtained with solution (2)."
          }
